--# Race Bib Logger v19.0.0
--
--v19 focuses on operational certainty: a volunteer must know why an exceptional passage is being accepted, command must see what needs reconciliation, and a device must not mark a batch synchronized unless the backend confirms the same bytes logically arrived.
--
--## Major additions
--
--- Auditable duplicate, unknown-runner, and route-exception decisions.
--- Structured reasons and reconciliation flags stored with each log.
--- A unified reconciliation queue and device/server confirmed-count comparison.
--- Blocking device-clock protection controlled through Setup.
--- Exact multi-store offline queue reporting and a race-day recovery wizard.
--- SHA-256 record/batch integrity checks and server acknowledgements.
--- Operational batch synchronization with retry backoff and BIB/incident priority.
--- Offline safety procedures, command timeline, COT alert deduplication, and checkpoint health.
--- Front-end modules, central state, typed contracts, reusable components, and stable error codes.
--- Automated asset validation, unit/static tests, Playwright scenarios, and a physical-device matrix.
--
--## Sheet changes
--
--`Racelog` expands from A:V to A:AC:
--
--- W Reason Code
--- X Reconciliation Flags
--- Y Route Exception Reason
--- Z Unknown BIB
--- AA Record Checksum
--- AB Edited At
--- AC Edited By
--
--Existing A:V values are preserved. During the one-time v19 schema migration, old optional helper content in W:AC is cleared because those columns become backend data.
--
--New auxiliary sheets are created as needed:
--
--- `SafetyAction`
--- `CheckpointStatus`
--
--`COTAlerts` gains reason, occurrence, first-seen, and last-seen columns.
--
--## Compatibility
--
--Legacy batch-sync requests without a checksum remain accepted for transitional compatibility, but v19 foreground and service-worker sync both send SHA-256 checksums. A v19 client requires a matching checksum acknowledgement before marking records synchronized.
