-+# Race Bib Logger v19.1.0 — Director Visibility and Entry Feedback
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+v19.1.0 improves command-centre awareness, safety-roster navigation, category reporting, and volunteer feedback without changing the v19.0.0 spreadsheet schema.
-+
-+## Implemented
-+
-+### Safety roster
-+
-+- Sort by **BIB** or **Last Seen** from the selector or by pressing the corresponding column heading.
-+- Press the active heading again to reverse ascending/descending order.
-+- BIB defaults to ascending; Last Seen defaults to newest first.
-+- The BIB column remains frozen while the roster is scrolled horizontally.
-+- Sort state is reflected with visible arrows and `aria-sort` metadata.
-+
-+### KM × category matrix
-+
-+- Matrix combinations now merge configured Setup rows with combinations actually observed in the roster.
-+- **Unspecified** distance and **Uncategorized** category are always represented.
-+- Unmatched records therefore remain visible instead of disappearing from the matrix.
-+
-+### Director category labels
-+
-+- Director charts, standings, category counts, and at-a-glance summaries now use a complete label in the form:
-+  - `80 KM · Women Open`
-+  - `35 KM · Women Open`
-+  - `Unspecified · Women Veteran`
-+- This prevents categories with the same name at different distances from being merged or shown ambiguously.
-+
-+### Compact command toolbar
-+
-+- Exit, log-status, Customize, and Refresh controls use compact icon-first buttons.
-+- Pressing a control reveals its full text for five seconds, then returns it to the compact state.
-+- Sync errors and active synchronization automatically reveal the status label.
-+- Exit uses a safer two-step action: first press reveals **Tap again to exit**; a second press within five seconds exits Director Mode.
-+
-+### Quick BIB entry duplicate feedback
-+
-+- While a BIB is being entered, the app checks whether that BIB has already been recorded.
-+- A repeated BIB changes to the same muted grey used for duplicate records and shows **Previously recorded**.
-+- The check is debounced and tokenized so rapid typing cannot apply an outdated result.
-+- Existing final duplicate-warning and override controls remain authoritative before submission.
-+
-+### GPS recording map
-+
-+- Added an offline, auto-fitted coordinate map to Director Mode.
-+- Shows each PWA device's latest GPS-tagged recording position.
-+- Shows up to the last 30 recorded GPS points as a trail per device.
-+- Shows configured checkpoint coordinates as square markers when available.
-+- Device markers indicate fresh, stale, or quiet activity by recency.
-+- Summary includes PWA device count, geotagged log count, checkpoint marker count, and newest GPS age.
-+- The map uses no third-party map tiles and does not transmit coordinates to an external mapping service.
-+
-+## Compatibility and data
-+
-+- No new Google Sheet columns or migration are introduced in v19.1.0.
-+- Existing v19.0.0 fields, reconciliation workflow, checksums, queue handling, safety data, and Apps Script endpoints are retained.
-+- App-shell cache names were advanced to v19.1.0 so clients receive the updated assets.
-+
-+## Deployment
-+
-+1. Back up the production sheet, Apps Script project, and offline queues.
-+2. Run `npm test` and require a complete pass.
-+3. Replace `Code.gs` and deploy a new Apps Script version.
-+4. Upload the complete PWA package, including `app/`, `icons/`, `index.html`, `manifest.json`, `sw.js`, and `tailwind.css`.
-+5. Open each device online once and confirm version 19.1.0 before field testing.
-+6. Complete the physical-device checks in `docs/DEVICE-TEST-MATRIX-v19.1.0.md`.
-+
-+## Field validation still required
-+
-+Local automated checks do not prove native iOS/Android PWA behavior, real GPS accuracy, live Apps Script/Google Sheets synchronization, background/foreground transitions, poor-network recovery, or long-duration race load. Those checks remain mandatory before production deployment.
