-+# Race Bib Logger v19.1.0 — Device Test Matrix
-+
-+Record device model, OS/browser version, installation mode, tester, date, and evidence for every run. A release is not race-day ready until every **Critical** row passes on physical hardware.
-+
-+| Priority | Platform / condition | Required checks | Pass criteria |
-+|---|---|---|---|
-+| Critical | Recent iPhone, installed PWA | Numeric entry, repeated-BIB grey state, duplicate modal, LOG, offline queue, reconnect | No clipped controls; repeat state appears before submission; final duplicate decision remains correct; all records reconcile |
-+| Critical | Older supported iPhone, installed PWA | Same flow plus 30-minute continuous entry | No reload, IndexedDB loss, stale duplicate colour, or progressive input lag |
-+| Critical | Recent Android Chrome, installed PWA | Full entry, background sync, Director Mode, GPS map | Checksummed records sync; device marker and age update correctly |
-+| Critical | Low-memory Android | 500 local records, Director Mode, Safety Log, reconnect | No crash; sorting and map remain responsive; reconciliation completes |
-+| Critical | iPhone and Android offline | Cold-open, enter 20 BIBs, incident, safety note, COT acknowledgement | App opens offline; queue counts are exact; records survive force-close |
-+| Critical | Poor network / packet loss | Repeated disconnects during sync and Director refresh | No duplicate writes; operational queues take priority; controls expose error state |
-+| Critical | Real GPS at multiple checkpoints | Logs from at least three PWAs and two configured checkpoint markers | Latest device positions, trails, recency states, counts, and markers are correct |
-+| Critical | GPS denied / timeout / weak accuracy | Log at configured checkpoint | Clear recovery path; approved fallback remains auditable; map does not fabricate coordinates |
-+| Critical | Safety roster horizontal scroll | Narrow phone viewport, drag horizontally across all columns | BIB header and BIB values remain frozen; rows stay aligned |
-+| Critical | Safety roster sorting | Sort BIB and Last Seen from selector and column headings | BIB defaults ascending; Last Seen defaults newest first; second press reverses; indicator and order agree |
-+| Critical | Matrix unmatched data | Records with missing KM, missing category, and both missing | Unspecified and Uncategorized cells appear with exact counts |
-+| Critical | Duplicate BIB race condition | Type, erase, and rapidly replace several BIBs | Debounced lookup never colours the wrong current BIB |
-+| High | Director toolbar on phone and tablet | Exit, status, Customize, Refresh | Icons are compact; labels show for about five seconds; first Exit press never closes; second press within window closes |
-+| High | Director full category labels | Same category at 35 KM, 80 KM, and 100 KM | Charts, standings, summaries, and category counts remain separated by KM |
-+| High | Director map with no GPS | Configured markers only, then no coordinates at all | Marker-only explanation is clear; fully empty state is clear; no external map request occurs |
-+| High | Director stale-device state | Device records aged 11 minutes and 31 minutes | Marker/legend changes to stale and quiet states at configured thresholds |
-+| High | Tablet portrait and landscape | Normal/minimal entry, Director, Safety roster | No inaccessible controls; map and matrix adapt without overlap |
-+| High | iPhone landscape / low-height viewport | Minimal keypad, duplicate warning, Director toolbar | Number keys, decisions, and critical Director actions remain reachable |
-+| High | Large-text accessibility | 125%, 150%, and 200% text size | Labels remain readable; icon buttons retain accessible names; primary actions do not overlap |
-+| High | Reduced motion | OS reduced-motion enabled | No essential state relies on animation or the five-second visual transition alone |
-+| High | Screen reader | Entry, repeated-BIB status, sortable headers, toolbar, map summary | Controls have meaningful names; sort state and status changes are announced |
-+| High | Privacy / network inspection | Use Director GPS map while monitoring requests | Coordinates are rendered locally; no map tiles or coordinates go to an unapproved third party |
-+| Medium | Bluetooth number pad | Digits, backspace, Enter, Escape | No double submission; duplicate lookup and focus are predictable |
-+| Medium | Two tabs on one device | Simultaneous entry, duplicate lookup, sorting, and sync | No record corruption; state converges after refresh |
-+| Medium | Battery saver / backgrounded PWA | Queue records, background, return to Director Mode | Foreground resume refreshes status and GPS age without manual repair |
-+| Medium | Storage pressure | IndexedDB near quota | Formal error code and recovery guidance appear; existing data is retained |
-+| Medium | Service-worker update | Upgrade v19.0.0 to v19.1.0 with queued logs | Queue survives cache rotation; v19.1.0 assets load offline |
-+| Medium | Command-centre display | Full-screen rotation, repeated refreshes, 1,000+ rows | No memory growth that affects operation; controls and widgets remain responsive |
-+
-+## Soak test
-+
-+Run at least two hours with three or more physical devices. Target at least 1,000 passages, intermittent connectivity, repeated BIB attempts, missing KM/category examples, GPS movement, two unknown BIBs, route overrides, incidents, safety updates, COT acknowledgements, a service-worker update, and horizontal Safety Log use. Verify zero pending records and matching server reconciliation counts at completion.
