--# Race Bib Logger v19.0.0 — Device Test Matrix
--
--Record device model, OS/browser version, installation mode, tester, date, and evidence for every run. A release is not race-day ready until all **Critical** rows pass on physical hardware.
--
--| Priority | Platform / condition | Required checks | Pass criteria |
--|---|---|---|---|
--| Critical | Recent iPhone, installed PWA | Numeric keypad, remark entry, duplicate modal, unknown BIB, route exception, LOG, offline queue, reconnect | No clipped controls; no phone keyboard in minimalist mode; exact queue counts; all records reconcile |
--| Critical | Older supported iPhone, installed PWA | Same flow plus 30-minute continuous entry | No tab reload, IndexedDB loss, or progressive input lag |
--| Critical | Recent Android Chrome, installed PWA | Full entry, background sync, notification-free resume | Checksummed batches confirm; operational records synchronize after BIB logs |
--| Critical | Low-memory Android | 500 local records, Director Mode, Safety Log, reconnect | No crash; entry remains responsive; reconciliation completes |
--| Critical | iPhone and Android offline | Cold-open from app shell, enter 20 BIBs, incident, safety note, COT ack | App opens offline; exact queue summary is accurate; records survive force-close |
--| Critical | Poor network / packet loss | Repeated disconnects during sync | No duplicate writes; exponential backoff; checksum mismatch never marks local records synced |
--| Critical | Clock drift | Device clock outside Setup threshold | Logging is blocked; connection retest updates the decision |
--| Critical | GPS denied / timeout / weak accuracy | Log at configured checkpoint | Clear recovery path; approved fallback is auditable; app does not freeze |
--| High | Tablet portrait and landscape | Normal and minimalist entry, Director Mode | No horizontal scrolling or inaccessible controls |
--| High | iPhone landscape / low-height viewport | Minimalist keypad and decision modal | Number keys, Cancel, and LOG remain reachable |
--| High | Large-text accessibility | 125%, 150%, 200% text size | Labels remain readable; primary actions do not overlap |
--| High | Reduced motion | OS reduced-motion enabled | No essential information relies on animation |
--| High | Screen reader | Setup, BIB entry, duplicate warning, clock block | Fields and dialogs have meaningful names and status changes announce |
--| High | Bluetooth number pad | Digits, backspace, Enter, Escape | No double submission; keyboard focus is predictable |
--| High | Two tabs on one device | Simultaneous foreground use and sync | No record corruption; duplicate detection remains consistent |
--| Medium | Battery saver / backgrounded PWA | Queue records, background, reconnect | Foreground resume continues sync without manual repair |
--| Medium | Storage pressure | IndexedDB near quota | Formal error code and recovery guidance appear; existing data is retained |
--| Medium | Service-worker update | Upgrade v18.0.10 to v19.0.0 with queued logs | Queue survives cache rotation; v19 modules and icons are available offline |
--| Medium | Event migration | Existing Racelog A:V data and optional W:X helpers | A:V is preserved; W:AC becomes v19 structured data; headers are correct |
--| Medium | Command centre | Timeline, checkpoint health, alert deduplication | Events are chronological; repeated alerts show occurrence count; statuses persist |
--| Medium | Safety action card | Online fetch then offline reopen | Emergency procedures, contacts, and checkpoint instructions remain visible |
--| Medium | Reconciliation | Unknown, duplicate, spam, edited, unsynced, server mismatch | Every group count and row is correct; server count is scoped to device creator ID |
--
--## Soak test
--
--Run at least two hours with three or more physical devices. Target at least 1,000 passages, intermittent connectivity, duplicate attempts, two unknown BIBs, route overrides, an incident, safety updates, COT acknowledgements, one clock-drift block, and one app-shell update. Export the final queue/reconciliation evidence and verify every device reports zero pending records.
