-+# Director Mode — 20 Recommended Next Improvements
-+
-+1. **Arrival surge forecast** — estimate the next 10-, 20-, and 30-minute runner volume at each checkpoint from current passage rates.
-+2. **Checkpoint load heatmap** — show scans per minute by checkpoint and time block so congestion is immediately visible.
-+3. **COT risk funnel** — group runners as safe, approaching cutoff, critical, overdue, acknowledged, and resolved.
-+4. **Missing-runner workflow** — assign an owner, record contact attempts, track search status, and preserve a complete timeline.
-+5. **Device operations map layer** — add battery, network state, pending queue, GPS age, and last sync to each PWA marker.
-+6. **Checkpoint staffing recommendation** — flag checkpoints where current volunteers are unlikely to handle the predicted arrival load.
-+7. **Route anomaly flow view** — visualize skipped checkpoints, reverse movement, improbable travel time, and approved route exceptions.
-+8. **Incident ownership and SLA timers** — assign each incident and display time to acknowledge, time responding, and time to resolve.
-+9. **Finish projection by distance/category** — estimate finish windows and counts using current runner progress and pace.
-+10. **DNS, DNF, withdrawal, and medical summary** — provide current totals, recent changes, and unresolved status records.
-+11. **Medical capacity panel** — track medic teams, available vehicles, active cases, destination, and availability state.
-+12. **Transport and sweep tracking** — show sweep teams, buses, pickup requests, passenger counts, and last known location.
-+13. **Weather risk panel** — optionally integrate official weather/lightning data and show event-defined escalation thresholds.
-+14. **Checkpoint supply status** — track water, ice, food, radios, lighting, first-aid stock, and resupply requests.
-+15. **Command announcements** — publish verified instructions to selected checkpoints or all PWAs with acknowledgement tracking.
-+16. **Shift handover snapshot** — generate a concise handover containing active incidents, missing runners, quiet devices, queues, and next COT.
-+17. **Director action audit log** — record filter changes, acknowledgements, overrides, status edits, and exports with operator identity.
-+18. **Saved command layouts** — allow Race Director, Safety, Timing, Medical, and Logistics views with role-specific widgets and filters.
-+19. **Full-screen operations rotation** — rotate selected widgets on a command-centre display while keeping critical alerts pinned.
-+20. **Post-race command report** — export timeline, checkpoint performance, incidents, COT outcomes, device uptime, and reconciliation status.
